title: "pallet-revive: Make the `limits` module public"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The `limits` module is now public, so tooling can read the limits the pallet enforces
      instead of copying them. The motivating user is `resolc`, which checks at link time
      whether a contract blob would pass `limits::code::enforce` on deployment and currently
      has to duplicate `BLOB_BYTES`, `BASIC_BLOCK_SIZE`, `INTERPRETER_CACHE_BYTES`,
      `PURGABLE_MEMORY_LIMIT`, `BASELINE_MEMORY_LIMIT` and `PAGE_SIZE`.

      No limit values change.
crates:
  - name: pallet-revive
    bump: minor
